.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/rdr2-vs-gg-differential.md:13:| **Embodiment (R2)** | ***real via strong incorporation*** — the involuntary **flinch/duck** at an on-screen threat (the thrown punch of the bar-fight, clip 10; a charging bear, clip 9): phantasia supplies the body so fully that the player's *real* body reacts to a flat image | *literal/eased* — bodily data supplied directly | **who supplies the body** — phantasia vs the medium |
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/rdr2-element-matrix.md:57:| **Animals-as-quarry** (deer, bear, legendary animal) [4, 9] | A2 — the quarry as determinate charged image fused with the kill-orekton; A4 the kill | Lud + Spa + Aff | Scene/Purpose (provision; legitimate violence) | nature (its fear/charge = co-agent's *orexis*); — | the predatory *technē* | the **charging bear** is the corpus's purest specimen of embodiment-as-flinch (R2 via phantasia, no HMD); "easier when they ain't shooting back" self-marks the low-flinch end |
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/rdr2-tutorial-RODA.md:121:- **The flinch = R2-via-phantasia.** Embodiment on the 2D pole registers as the **involuntary flinch** at an on-screen threat — phantasia supplies the body so fully that the player's *real* body reacts to a flat image. The cleanest specimens: the **charging bear** (clip 9, 11:00–12:30 — "the single cleanest specimen in the playthrough of embodiment-registered-as-flinch, no HMD") and the **bar-fight** (clip 10, the thrown punch, 02:33–03:16 — symbolic button input, zero haptic, the only somatic register the flinch). Sustained dialogue-free flinch fields: the O'Driscoll raid (clip 11, 08:30–14:00) and the Strawberry jailbreak onset (clip 15, 03:30–04:30). "Look out!" (clip 3b, 07:08) is where the flinch first fires in the curriculum.
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/rdr2-tutorial-RODA.md:131:> Across ~6.7 hours of early-game play, *Red Dead Redemption 2* runs not a single actualization but a **protracted sedimentation**: it engineers a **dual *hexis*-bundle** — a technē-hexis (horsemanship, gunplay, tracking, heist- and minigame-craft, demonstrated at ceiling in clip 9) and, underneath and primary to it, an **ethical-hexis** (gang-loyalty installed in the opening cutscene before the stick is held, clip 1 04:11; belonging-through-labor dwelt by repetition in camp, clips 6a–d; the contributive creed and out-group ruthlessness of clip 5; the honor-scored moral self of clips 3a/7/8; and finally theft-as-livelihood, clip 16's fence-unlock). The orekton is re-pitched three times — blizzard-survival → standing/belonging → the outlaw economy — and drawn through the A₀→A₄ chain by a desire the design first *posits* (camp scarcity, clip 4 00:58) and then *collectivizes* (the camp "gets its slice," clip 5 65:00). The **honor system is a partial, external motive-attribution machine**, diagnostically *selective*: **inert** on the maximal/intimate choke-or-spare fork (clip 3a 11:31, where a tolling bell is the only residue of a withheld score) yet **active** on socially-witnessed excess (clip 10's bar-fight, Trelawney's "you won the fight already," 05:23) and faction-coded killing (clip 11's near-free O'Driscoll violence; clip 15's honor cost for killing lawmen) — it launders motive toward *scene/purpose* and privatizes collective acts onto the lone agent. *Bia* structures the arc as a rhythm of agent→patient inversions — the cinematic baseline (clip 1), the whiteout-masked leash (clip 2), inflicted cruelty (Kieran, clip 5 27:25; the bounty hogtie, clip 8 12:00), suffered loosening (the drunk-cam, clip 12; the narrative compulsion to free a treacherous ally, clip 15) — and, decisively, *reversed* in the rescue that restores Sean's agency (clip 14 10:30), the mirror of the cruelty it answers; against all of which the camp's voluntary labor and clip 16's prohairesis-preserving plan stand as the anti-*bia* counter-pole. Incorporation reaches **both** disclosednesses: world-disclosedness by **phantasmatic subtraction** earned through sheer world-density, and — the key advance over *Gnomes & Goblins* — **co-disclosedness consummated as the acting-together "WE"** (the jointly-sourced heist, raid, and rescue) that G&G held at the threshold. As the **2D / large-data-discrepancy / high-phantasia-load** pole, RDR2 supplies the body entirely through phantasia: embodiment is the **involuntary flinch** (R2-via-phantasia: the charging bear, clip 9; the thrown punch, clip 10), the felt load is maximal where on-screen data is thinnest (the whiteout, clip 2; the drunk-cam, clip 12), and the design *compensates* the discrepancy with a battery of 2D rhetorical instruments — Eagle-Eye, Dead-Eye, the honor meter, and the watching cinematic camera — that do the eidetic, affective, and moral work a body or an HMD would otherwise carry. The whole bundle is, in Layer-5 terms, the **slow A₄→A₀′ carry-over** that builds the desiring, dwelling, morally-scored agent the later capstone (the Sonny scene, outside clips 1–16) ruptures and partially supplants: the rupture has ontological force *only because* this protracted cultivation has already laid down the disposition there is to rupture — the 2D route to incorporation differing from the VR route in *how*, not *whether*.
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-traces/RDR2 - 09 - Horse, Bear Hunt, Legendary Animal -- beatmap.md:20:| 11:00–12:30 | `[INFER]` **The bear charges** → involuntary flinch; possible maul (forced takedown animation) → return fire (rifle / Dead Eye). [VISUAL: bear rears + sprints at camera; if maul — Arthur knocked prone, control stripped; muzzle flashes; bear drops] | **A3→A4 under threat + BIA.** A3 = doxa concretized with fear; A4 = the kill. **If the maul fires, it is *bia*** — a forced animation, agent→patient inversion, agency stripped. This is the **flinch apex (R2 via phantasia).** | **LOAD-BEARING 2D MOMENT.** The charging bear is the clip's purest specimen of *embodiment-as-flinch*: the involuntary recoil at an on-screen predator, with no HMD — the felt body is entirely phantasia-supplied. |
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-traces/RDR2 - 09 - Horse, Bear Hunt, Legendary Animal -- beatmap.md:32:This clip is the corpus's **apex specimen of the *techne*-hexis bundle**: the skill-disposition seeded under Charles's narration in clip 4 ("get your eye in," "good tension on the string") here runs **untutored and at ceiling** across two crafts at once — horsemanship (gait, calm-the-mount, the cultivated bond) and the hunter's eye-and-hand (track → study → shot-placement → harvest). Where clip 4 was the *seeding* and was legible because a tutor voiced each stage, clip 09 is the *demonstration*, and its silence is diagnostic: the absence of any dialogue (the transcript is pure Whisper "you" padding) is exactly what a mature *hexis* looks like — no longer narrated, only enacted. The protracted disposition it advances is therefore the **self-directed craftsman's competence**, and its distinctive contribution beyond clip 4 is the **animal as co-agent**: the mount, the bear, and the legendary quarry each carry their own *orexis*, so the clip is also where RODA's actualization-of-desire meets a *second* desiring agent on screen. The **horse-bond** (05:00–07:30) is the positive pole of RDR2's animal-treatment register — the same axis the honor-system penalizes when a player abuses a horse — so the care-act here, though it posts no honor toast, *models the ethical disposition* the motive-machine tracks elsewhere; the bond sits between technē and ethics (care toward an animal). The **ethical/agency forks** are two, both on the co-agency seam: (1) the **horse-rear** (02:30–05:00), a soft agent/patient inversion where the animal's fear interrupts the player's act and demands re-attunement; and (2) the **bear/legendary charge** (11:00–12:30, 18:30–20:30), where a maul or knock-down — if the frames show the forced-prone animation — is genuine **bia**: control stripped, the hunter momentarily made patient by the hunted. The **honor-motive attribution** stays quiet and legitimate (hunting-for-provision = **scene/purpose**, as in clip 4), with the legendary kill adding a **mastery/agent** overlay (the trophy-pelt, the Trapper economy). For the VR-2D thesis this clip is doubly load-bearing: the **charging bear** is the single cleanest specimen in the playthrough of *embodiment-registered-as-flinch* (R2 via phantasia, no HMD, the felt body supplied entirely behind stick/button), and the clip stacks the game's three **phantasia-prostheses** — Eagle Eye (tracking-vision), the legendary aura-filter (specialness-as-UI), and Dead Eye (composure-as-time-slow) — each a 2D compensation for an eidetic/affective state a body would otherwise hold, precisely where a VR counterpart (Gnomes & Goblins) would begin to deliver it proprioceptively.
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-read-verification.md:16:| **9** bear (full clip scanned 2026-06-27) | bear-charge flinch / maul | **RESOLVED — no flinch/maul** | The mission is "Exit Pursued by a Bruised Ego," the **comedic scripted-*escape*** hunt: the Legendary Bear rears up briefly (~22:47) then **breaks off** ("discovered a Legendary Animal — return to track it"); both men unharmed, joking ("That was fun"). **No maul / agent→patient inversion, no Dead-Eye, no shooting-under-threat.** → clip 9 is the hunt-**ritual** (tracking, bait-crafting, the **Eagle-Eye** perception-prosthesis, the ambush setup) + a thwarted-bear comedy — **NOT a flinch/embodiment specimen** (so correct the matrix's "charging bear = purest flinch" → the flinch anchor is the bar-fight/combat, not the bear). *(Caution: the desaturated frames are inventory radial menus, not Dead-Eye.)* |
.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z/tree/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-read-verification.md:27:- **Bear (9): RESOLVED** — the comedic scripted-*escape* hunt; no maul/flinch. Clip 9 = the hunt-ritual + thwarted-bear comedy, not an embodiment specimen. (The matrix's "charging bear = purest flinch" is corrected; the flinch anchor is the bar-fight/combat.)
plans/packs/rdr2-section5-foundation-snapshot-2026-07-03.tex:137:It was built, moreover, by the route the flat screen makes necessary, and that route is the chapter's contribution to the differential the two cases compose. Where the head-mounted world of \textit{Gnomes \& Goblins} hands the body its surround and asks little of the image, the screen withholds the surround and asks everything — the cold of the blizzard, the heft of the drawn bow, the lurch of the leaping train, the recoil from the charging bear, each supplied by the player's own \textit{phantasia} across a data-discrepancy the medium never closes. And where the eye alone will not suffice, the design lends prostheses — Eagle Eye for the tracker's gaze, Dead Eye for the marksman's composure, the drunk-cam for the swimming head — the 2D pole's standing instruments of compensation. The disposition deposited is the same kind of thing the virtual-reality world deposited at the other pole, an incorporation that sediments into a \textit{hexis}. What differs is only the road to it, and that road, in the screen-based case, runs through the image and not the body. The VR pole reaches its dwelling by giving the body its world; the 2D pole reaches the same dwelling by making the player imagine one.
tmp/Dissertation/Part_II/Part-II-COMBINED-v1-2026-06-30.md:508:It was built, moreover, by the route the flat screen makes necessary, and that route is the chapter's contribution to the differential the two cases compose. Where the head-mounted world of *Gnomes & Goblins* hands the body its surround and asks little of the image, the screen withholds the surround and asks everything — the cold of the blizzard, the heft of the drawn bow, the lurch of the leaping train, the recoil from the charging bear, each supplied by the player's own *phantasia* across a data-discrepancy the medium never closes. And where the eye alone will not suffice, the design lends prostheses — Eagle Eye for the tracker's gaze, Dead Eye for the marksman's composure, the drunk-cam for the swimming head — the 2D pole's standing instruments of compensation. The disposition deposited is the same kind of thing the virtual-reality world deposited at the other pole, an incorporation that sediments into a *hexis*. What differs is only the road to it, and that road, in the screen-based case, runs through the image and not the body. The VR pole reaches its dwelling by giving the body its world; the 2D pole reaches the same dwelling by making the player imagine one.
tmp/Dissertation/Part_II/Part-II-COMBINED-v2-2026-07-01.tex:541:It was built, moreover, by the route the flat screen makes necessary, and that route is the chapter's contribution to the differential the two cases compose. Where the head-mounted world of \textit{Gnomes \& Goblins} hands the body its surround and asks little of the image, the screen withholds the surround and asks everything — the cold of the blizzard, the heft of the drawn bow, the lurch of the leaping train, the recoil from the charging bear, each supplied by the player's own \textit{phantasia} across a data-discrepancy the medium never closes. And where the eye alone will not suffice, the design lends prostheses — Eagle Eye for the tracker's gaze, Dead Eye for the marksman's composure, the drunk-cam for the swimming head — the 2D pole's standing instruments of compensation. The disposition deposited is the same kind of thing the virtual-reality world deposited at the other pole, an incorporation that sediments into a \textit{hexis}. What differs is only the road to it, and that road, in the screen-based case, runs through the image and not the body. The VR pole reaches its dwelling by giving the body its world; the 2D pole reaches the same dwelling by making the player imagine one.
tmp/Dissertation/Part_II/Part-II-COMBINED-v4-2026-07-15.tex:586:It was built, moreover, by the route the flat screen makes necessary, and that route is the chapter's contribution to the differential the two cases compose. Where the head-mounted world of \textit{Gnomes \& Goblins} hands the body its surround and asks little of the image, the screen withholds the surround and asks everything — the cold of the blizzard, the heft of the drawn bow, the lurch of the leaping train, the recoil from the charging bear, each supplied by the player's own \textit{phantasia}. Where the eye alone will not suffice, the design lends instruments: Eagle Eye for the tracker's gaze, Dead Eye for the marksman's composure. The disposition deposited is the same kind of thing the virtual-reality world deposited in its player, an incorporation that sediments into a \textit{hexis}; what differs is the road. The screen-based route runs through the image and through what the player makes of it — the design does its work by shaping the player's cognitive orientations, seeding the \textit{phantasmata} under which its world appears, and steering the \textit{doxai} the player forms about that world, reaching the disposition through opinion where the headset reaches it through the body.
